WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.010
Speaker 1: But let me tell you something else.

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:06.240
The most important thing that needs to happen
and this is the final thing I want to talk

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.350
about on today's show, today's main show.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:15.160
And that is that I think this January six
select committee, the Riot Committee, whatever

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.800
you want to call it.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.340
They're now in over their heads.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:30.189
I do not think this committee, as it is right
now, should be the lead investor investigatory

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:33.900
body into the Capitol riot.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.860
I believe that it is time for Merrick Garland
to finally step up.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:48.220
And appoint a special prosecutor to officially
start a criminal investigation into these

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.220
events.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:54.790
Now, don't get me wrong, so far, for the most
part, I have been very happy with what the

00:00:54.790 --> 00:01:00.280
select committee has done and the reason I
say they're in over their heads is because

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:06.470
of the sheer scope of what it is they're trying
to do, which, to be honest, we don't even

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:10.070
really know everything they're attempting
to do yet.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:14.760
So, you know, we have to contend with that.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.970
You know, they've got Trump out there, they
said, Oh, we may be looking at criminal activity

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.670
here, we may be looking at criminal activity
with these individuals.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.660
We got Roger Stone, we got Steve Bannon now.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:27.900
We got members of Congress.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.920
And they can't even if they're from opposing
parties, heck, almost especially if they're

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:41.280
from opposing parties, they now really can't
do this in a nonpartizan way because you do

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:48.250
have lawmakers that do have to answer these
questions, they absolutely have to.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:53.760
That's why a special prosecutor is now needed,
convene a grand jury and essentially take

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.310
it over for the most part.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:03.479
Because the optics are always going to be
bad if you have a Democrat controlled committee

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:08.479
subpoenaing Republican members of Congress,
Republicans are going to weaponize that to

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:10.720
show that, oh, the whole thing is a Partizan
sham.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:14.580
Look, they're going after our lawmakers because
this is so ridiculous.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:19.590
Even though there's legitimate reason to go
after them, a special prosecutor could avoid

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:20.590
that.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:25.160
To a degree, they're still going to claim
it's Partizan witch hunt.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:31.210
But the bigger problem is the longevity of
this committee.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:36.280
This committee is not going to be able to
wrap up this investigation by the midterms.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.280
They're just not.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.840
And if they do wrap up before then, then they've
cut corners in a lot of places and it's not

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.209
a complete investigation.

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:48.480
Special prosecutor avoids that problem.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.860
Because what happens when Republicans win
back the House, if they win back the House,

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.700
they kill the committee, it's over.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.200
They disband it.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.080
And what happens if members of the committee
don't win reelection?

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:06.910
Well, then you're in for a real big problem
to a special prosecutor appointed by the attorney

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:11.110
general avoids all of those problems.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:15.819
The Republicans wouldn't be able to squash
a special prosecutor, we've seen them try.

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:17.560
Trust me, we have.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:21.290
But they weren't successful with it.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:24.140
So that's what needs to happen now.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:29.800
But 100 percent of that rests upon the shoulders
of Attorney General Merrick Garland, who is

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.860
apparently just made it clear he's not going
to do anything.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.900
And for the record, part of the reason why
I say that there's no way this committee can

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.531
even wrap things up by the midterms or even
by next January, when the new Congress would

00:03:40.531 --> 00:03:41.580
be sworn in.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.950
Steve Bannon doesn't even go on trial for
contempt until July.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.629
OK.

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:50.600
You're not going to have resolution for that.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:55.580
Mark Meadows hasn't even been arrested yet,
so he'll be arrested or arraigned, and then

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:59.319
they'll set a trial, which will likely be
even further out from July.

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:04.480
So you're not going to get the cooperation
you need from these people.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:10.590
Probably until after the election, because
if they lose the cases, they're going to appeal.

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:15.560
So this committee is doomed from the start
because of the way Congress itself is set

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:16.820
up.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.250
But you avoid those problems.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.919
A lot of them disappear completely.

00:04:22.919 --> 00:04:30.680
If the thing is handed over to a special prosecutor
or multiple special prosecutors, you know,

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.680
appoint several.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:36.199
There's really no limit to how many you could
appoint to handle each different aspect of

00:04:36.199 --> 00:04:37.199
that.

00:04:37.199 --> 00:04:40.469
The rally organizers could be one focus of
one prosecutor.

00:04:40.469 --> 00:04:43.189
The Trump administration could be another.

00:04:43.189 --> 00:04:45.249
The members of Congress could be another.

00:04:45.249 --> 00:04:49.379
And then, of course, all the outside players
who weren't with the rally, they weren't with

00:04:49.379 --> 00:04:50.940
the administration or Congress.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:58.780
You know, you're Bannon's, you're Fox News
hosts who have been texting with Mark.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:00.919
All of those other individuals could fall
or another one.

00:05:00.919 --> 00:05:02.000
So there you go.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.240
But anyway, listen, we're out of time for
today's show.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.930
I'm Farron Cousins.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:09.490
Find me on social media at fair and balanced.

